* Week 8: ARB starts at the null match and extends by exactly one
* character each time the rest of the pattern fails to follow it
* (research/snobol/03-pattern-matching.md, `ARB = NULL | LEN(1) *ARB`).
* Against "MOUNTAIN", `"O" ARB "A"` must skip exactly "UNT" -- the
* shortest run of characters between the "O" and the next "A" -- not
* jump straight to the first "A" it could plausibly stop before, and
* not stop short of it either. Run with --trace to watch ARB retry at
* length 0, 1, 2, 3 in turn before "A" finally follows.
        SUBJECT = 'MOUNTAIN'
        SUBJECT 'O' ARB 'A'    :F(NOMATCH)
        OUTPUT = 'ARB FOUND THE GAP'   :(STOP)
NOMATCH OUTPUT = 'NO MATCH'
STOP    SUBJECT = SUBJECT
